  "title": "browsing collages",
  "subtext": "a collection of sketches made with found browsing materials",
  "descriptionMd": "*browsing collages* are sketches made entirely using materials found while browsing (images, buttons, headings, etc.) saved by [we were online](https://spencer.place/creation/we-were-online/).\n&nbsp;\nEvery element keeps its provenance, so anything in a collage can be traced back to the page (and the people) it came from. Each collage becomes an artifact representing a browsing session, the questions and interests I chased, arranged into a meaningful composition.\n&nbsp;\nInspired by David Hockney’s [photographic collages](https://www.hockney.com/index.php/works/photos/photographic-collages), these found forms explore the everyday, personal imagery that makes up so much of our internet life.",
